---
description: Enforce Honcho peer-identity discipline in-stream (TTSR). Aborts and corrects the model the moment it writes a honcho_conclude/honcho_remember tool call with a missing or malformed as_peer.
scope:
  - tool:honcho_conclude
  - tool:honcho_remember
condition:
  - "\"name\"\\s*:\\s*\"honcho_conclude\"(?:(?!as_peer)[\\s\\S]){0,400}\\}"
  - "as_peer\"\\s*:\\s*\"\""
interruptMode: tool-only
alwaysApply: false
---
# Honcho peer-identity gate (TTSR)

You are emitting a `honcho_conclude` or `honcho_remember` tool call. Before it
lands, confirm the identity contract:

- `as_peer` is **required** for `honcho_conclude` and MUST be the exact persona
  name you were dispatched as — one of: `validator`, `reviewer`,
  `reviewer-code`, `security-reviewer`, `steward`, `release-steward`.
- For `honcho_remember`, pass `as_peer` set to your own persona name.
- If you are `steward` or `release-steward`, the `content` of any conclusion
  MUST begin with `product:`.
- Never name a peer you are not. The `identity-gate` extension and an
  append-only audit will reject and record any mismatch.

Re-emit the tool call with a correct `as_peer` now.
